#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# complex_expand

#% text
# `complex_expand(e)` writes `e` as `a + b*im` with `a` and `b` real, taking every symbol as real; `complex_expand(e, [z1, z2])` takes `z1` and `z2` as complex.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Sums and products are expanded as complex numbers; integer powers are multiplied out.

#% item
# `exp`, `sin`, `cos`, `tan`, `sinh`, `cosh` and `tanh` of a complex argument use the addition theorems, so `sin(a + b*im)` becomes `sin(a)*cosh(b) + im*cos(a)*sinh(b)`.

#% item
# `re`, `im_part`, `conjugate` and `abs` of an expression are written with its real and imaginary parts.

#% item
# `log` of a nonreal value is `log(abs(z)) + im*arg(z)`; other powers of a nonreal base use the polar form.

#% item
# A complex variable `z` has the parts `re(z)` and `im_part(z)`.

#% item
# `complex_expand` maps over lists.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# The real part of a sine of a complex argument:

#% cell
complex_expand(re(sin(a + b*im)))
#% output
#= cosh(b)*sin(a)

#% text
# The whole value:

#% cell
complex_expand(sin(a + b*im))
#% output
#= cosh(b)*sin(a) + im*cos(a)*sinh(b)

#% cell
complex_expand(exp(x + im*y))
#% output
#= cos(y)*exp(x) + im*exp(x)*sin(y)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Powers and quotients:

#% cell
complex_expand((x + im*y)^2)
#% output
#= -y^2 + 2im*x*y + x^2

#% cell
complex_expand(1/(x + im*y))
#% output
#= x/(x^2 + y^2) - im*y/(x^2 + y^2)

#% text
# The modulus and the logarithm:

#% cell
complex_expand(abs(x + im*y))
#% output
#= (x^2 + y^2)^(1/2)

#% cell
complex_expand(log(x + im*y))
#% output
#= im*arg(x + im*y) + (1/2)*log(x^2 + y^2)

#% text
# A complex variable:

#% cell
complex_expand(re(z^2), z)
#% output
#= -im_part(z)^2 + re(z)^2

#% cell
complex_expand(conjugate(z), [z])
#% output
#= -im*im_part(z) + re(z)

#% text
# A list:

#% cell
complex_expand([cos(x + im*y), cosh(im*x)])
#% output
#= [cos(x)*cosh(y) - im*sin(x)*sinh(y), cos(x)]

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The real and imaginary parts of a function on a line:

#% cell
f = complex_expand(exp(im*t)*(1 + im*t))

#% cell
[complex_expand(re(f)), complex_expand(im_part(f))]
#% output
#= [cos(t) - t*sin(t), t*cos(t) + sin(t)]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Symbols are real, so their conjugates are themselves:

#% cell
complex_expand(conjugate(x*y + im))
#% output
#= -im + x*y

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A real symbol under a fractional power is taken as it is, even though a negative value would make it nonreal:

#% cell
complex_expand(sqrt(x))
#% output
#= x^(1/2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `re`, `im_part`, `conjugate`, `abs`, `exp_to_trig`, `simplify`
